D2 - DESIGN BRIEF
=================

PROJECT OVERVIEW
----------------
Working title: FuelFare

FuelFare is a trip cost calculator. Users pick their vehicle,
enter a start and destination, and see what the trip will cost in gas
using their car's official fuel economy and the local gas price. It
redesigns the vehicle lookup in NRCan's Fuel Consumption Ratings Search
Tool into a simple, guided tool focused on one question: "What will this
trip cost me?"


PROBLEM STATEMENT
-----------------
The NRCan tool has the right data but is hard to use. Too many filters appear at once, selecting more than one option needs a keyboard shortcut, and the Model list stays empty without explaining why. Drivers who just
want to know their car's fuel cost have to work through a dense government form, and it does not work well on a phone.


TARGET USERS
------------
1. Daily commuters (students and workers)
   Needs:  know weekly or monthly gas costs, split costs with carpools.
   Tasks:  save their vehicle, calculate a regular trip, save that trip.

2. Occasional road-trippers
   Needs:  budget gas for a longer trip before leaving.
   Tasks:  enter a start and destination, pick a vehicle, see total cost.


REDESIGN OBJECTIVES
-------------------
1. Users can start a calculation with 3 fields or fewer
   (fixes Problem 1: too many filters).
2. Every control works by tap or click, with no keyboard shortcuts needed
   (fixes Problem 2: Ctrl/Command multi-select).
3. The vehicle picker guides users step by step, Make -> Model -> Year,
   with clear prompts at each step (fixes Problem 3: empty Model list).


SCOPE
-----
In scope:
- Home page with the trip calculator
- Trip Results page
- My Garage (save and choose a vehicle)
- Saved Trips
- Responsive layouts for mobile, tablet and desktop

Out of scope / deferred:
- Live gas prices from an outside service (users enter the price for now)
- User accounts and sign-in
- Reading real fuel, rpms and speed from the car with a  (OBD-II) and an esp32 with a screen


CONSTRAINTS AND ASSUMPTIONS
---------------------------
Brand:Use the WS03A colour system (red #D72638 with neutrals) and the WS03B typography system (Inter).
Content:Fuel economy comes from NRCan's open fuel consumption ratings data.
Technical:Final site is hosted on GitHub Pages, which is static, so there is no backend or database.
Accessibility:  Meet WCAG AA contrast (4.5:1 body text, 3:1 large text) and 44px minimum touch targets.
Time:One semester, built across M1 to the final redesign.
Assumption:Users know their vehicle's make, model and year, but notits fuel economy. (Not yet tested.)


SUCCESS CRITERIA
----------------
1. A first-time user can calculate a trip cost in under 1 minute without help.
2. A tester can find and choose their vehicle on a phone without getting stuck.
3. All text and buttons pass WCAG AA contrast checks.
4. Testers can correctly state the trip's total cost after viewing the results page.